messages.content:
Prithee, good host, restrain thy tempest! Thy quest for savory vittles shall yet find fruit. Thou seek’st vegetarian fare fit for the open flame? Herein lieth counsel most steadfast:

- Corn on the cob, parboiled soft, then roasted till the kernels smolder and sweeten, anointed with herb-laced butter;
- Firm tofu, brushed with soy and sesame, seared on the grate till golden, then tossed with scallions and chili-ginger;
- Halloumi squares, marinated in garlic and oregano, grilled till crisp-edged and golden, served atop a bed of minted couscous;
- Portobello caps, rubbed with balsamic glaze, grilled flesh-side down till they puff and brown, ready for a squeeze of lemon;
- Pineapple chunks, skewered with red pepper and onion, kissed by the fire till caramelized, a sweet counterpoint to the smoke.

Thus shall thy guests, whether of meat or of leaf, find plenty to please. Prithee, trust in these humble recipes, and thy barbecue shall be merry indeed.

